    "calculation_rules": {
      "input": "Recompute all quantities from the pinned public historical native members and the paper/SI targets; do not copy or trust candidate aggregates.",
      "row_scope": "Only ES bond reference items with a non-null target for the route are included. There are 13 tracked bond identities; PBE0 and ADMM each have 13 rows, sTDA has 10 rows because the three M14 default targets are null. The per-method published reference mapping is explicit: conventional PBE0 uses SI Table 3 PBE0|TZVP; ADMM-PBE0 uses SI Table 3 ADMM|TZVP+tzp; sTDA uses SI Table 14 sTDA@PBE0|TZVP. All vs_eom_ccsd rows use the paired SI Table 3 EOM-CCSD column (refs.json values.CCSD); Table 14 sTDA values are never substituted as EOM-CCSD references.",
      "vs_eom_ccsd": "For each route row, delta_pm = computed_mean_pm - the matched SI Table 3 EOM-CCSD value (refs.json values.CCSD); for Table 14 sTDA rows, pair by the same normalized molecule and bond label. Calculate signed mean, mean absolute error (MAE), maximum absolute delta, and all ref_id values exactly tied at the maximum absolute delta.",
      "same_method_paper_residual": "For each route row, delta_pm = computed_mean_pm - that route's published method value: PBE0 and ADMM from their distinct SI Table 3 CP2K columns; sTDA from SI Table 14 sTDA@PBE0/TZVP column. Calculate the same four statistics.",
      "admm_minus_pbe0": "For each of 13 tracked ES bond identities, delta_pm = ADMM-PBE0 computed_mean_pm - conventional PBE0 computed_mean_pm; then calculate the same four statistics.",
      "stats": "count is the number of rows; signed_mean_pm is arithmetic mean(delta_pm); mae_pm is arithmetic mean(abs(delta_pm)); max_abs_pm is max(abs(delta_pm)); worst_ref_ids contains every reference row id exactly tied at max_abs_pm, sorted lexically by the canonical builder (the verifier compares this field as a set).",
      "precision": "Use Decimal arithmetic for summary aggregation. Serialize finite summary numeric measurements as decimal strings rounded to exactly 9 fractional digits using decimal ROUND_HALF_EVEN; the verifier accepts parsed numeric differences <= 5e-10 pm. Determine maximum ties from unrounded Decimal deltas before serialization. CSV computed geometry/residual display tolerance is 0.02 pm and published/SI value display tolerance is 1e-9 pm; these are representation checks only.",
      "decimal_rounding_mode": "ROUND_HALF_EVEN"
    }
  },
